list.item:
surat (to write), the similar verbals as above, so far as the idea of the root and the use permit, with this variant:

susurátan, not sururátan,

susuráton, not sururáton;

div.p:
57  However, the correct and proper form is the first, Panalaron, a verbal derived from panalad  a plural infinitive of the verb pagsálad  which means “to sound”. The said suburb of Tacloban, it is believed took this name from the fact that, anciently, the people used to sound (
                     panálad
                     )  in such place which was then covered by the sea. ↑
